The mechanical artifacts are internally self-consistent, but the mathematical gate fails. Operational K follows `VERIFICATION → CONNECTION-RULE → VERIFICATION-BASE`; that closure contains two load-bearing simplification rules that are domain lemmas. Removing either makes the fresh bridge-free proof stop at precisely the missing equation, so the selected zero-obligation generation is not legitimate. I’m writing the self-contained review and final evidence index now.
